      "id": "disable-expression",
      "basis": [
        "TaskCommentInput.tsx:50-53,291-330",
        "useTaskDetailSession.ts:106-160"
      ],
      "finding": "The actual textarea receives disabled = session.submitPending || !controller.isOwner. ComposerSurface, MentionableTextarea and AutoResizeTextarea forward this prop. isOwner depends on enabled, context/switching, live Team availability, ready phase, null deletion intent, matching nondeleted current Task and exact owner surface. The captured probe omits several operands and rendered controller state when owner extraction returns null.",
      "classification": "exact source fact; which operand changed in the original blur is unobserved"
    },
    {
      "id": "owner-extractor",
      "basis": [
        "desktop-task-comment-input-target.ts:10-47",
        "desktop-task-board-attachments-ui.ts:214-255"
      ],
      "finding": "ownerPresent=false means the strict current-fiber/controller/input expression returned null. It filters controller.isOwner, controller/task/identity equality, owner surface, visible enabled textarea and exact same controller reference in the input ancestry. It does not mean stored ownerSurfaceId became null. Current-fiber/ancestry and reference checks can refuse without exposing their reason.",
      "classification": "exact source semantics; no claim that reflection itself caused this failure"
    },
    {
      "id": "specific-authority-invalidation-candidate",
      "basis": [
        "createHostTeamChanges.ts:122-198",
        "store/index.ts:1543-1578",
        "taskDetailReadAuthority.ts:333-338,372-411",
        "teamTaskDetailSlice.ts:396-437",
        "taskDetailReadModel.ts:71-76",
        "taskDetailReadAuthority.ts:192-201,299-314",
        "useTaskDetailSession.ts:106-160"
      ],
      "finding": "For fresh Host product feed events, gap or resync, the existing shared loop emits config and inbox full-read invalidations. An accepted config event calls invalidateTaskDetailTeamSource, deletes the accepted live Team snapshot and marks the detail refresh pending while retaining its full object/phase. isTaskDetailTeamUnavailable can then be true and render isOwner false without changing ownerSurfaceId or ownerRevision. A later accepted scoped snapshot can permit ownership again. Ordinary polls without product/conversation change do not fabricate a config event.",
      "classification": "concrete reachable source mechanism and strongest causal candidate; no original feed-event/authority-revision/callback timestamp joins the observed blur"
    },
    {
      "id": "draft-hydration-distinction",
      "basis": [
        "useTaskDetailSession.ts:215-248",
        "taskDetailSession.ts:89-106"
      ],
      "finding": "The ordinary persisted draft hydrate only conditionally updates comment text/chips at revision zero; it has no direct focus call and does not itself set submitPending or the owner surface. It must not be named the demonstrated reason for disabled=true.",
      "classification": "exact source exclusion of a direct hydrate-to-disable assignment, not universal exclusion of all surrounding asynchronous work"
    },
    {
      "id": "dom-retention-and-remount",
      "basis": [
        "TeamDetailView.tsx:250-380",
        "TaskDetailDialog.tsx:82-136,248-305",
        "TaskDetailContent.tsx:64-101",
        "TaskDetailBody.tsx:492-534",
        "CollapsibleTeamSection.tsx:72-95,215-238",
        "ComposerSurface.tsx:19-44",
        "MentionableTextarea.tsx:1343-1353",
        "auto-resize-textarea.tsx:64-87"
      ],
      "finding": "The selected Task identity and surface are stable refs/state; loaded TaskDetailContent is keyed by the same identity, the Comments section defaults open, and the textarea has no key derived from ownerRevision or isOwner. Disabling alone does not select a different JSX textarea. Losing the full Task, closing/remounting ancestors or collapsing Comments could replace it, but no original node-continuity or component lifecycle trace proves that. Existing wrapper height work does not restore focus on re-enable.",
      "classification": "source route analysis; a stable key is not runtime Node identity proof"
    },
    {
      "id": "focus-scope-candidate",
      "basis": [
        "dialog.tsx:35-69",
        "TaskDetailDialog.tsx:248-265",
        "local @radix-ui/react-dialog 1.1.15 dist/index.mjs:130-159,204-233",
        "local patched @radix-ui/react-focus-scope 1.1.7 dist/index.mjs:56-91,92-122"
      ],
      "finding": "The normal open modal traps focus. The inspected FocusScope implementation returns on focusout with relatedTarget null; its child-list MutationObserver, when document.activeElement is BODY, focuses the container if any observed mutation removed a descendant. That removal need not be the textarea. Its next focusin records the DIV as lastFocusedElement. It has no separate textarea-re-enabled restoration rule. This can explain BODY then DIV after an earlier focus loss, but the original receipt has no mutation list, relatedTarget or callback tag.",
      "classification": "source-supported explanation; actual fallback invocation unproved"
    },
    {
      "id": "existing-ref-patch",
      "basis": [
        "pnpm-lock.yaml:100-106,16065-16085,16133-16142",
